Google Calendar rules:
- Do not create duplicate DailyFlow calendars.
- Before creating a DailyFlow calendar, always check whether one already exists and reuse it.
- DailyFlow-created events should be created only inside the dedicated DailyFlow Google Calendar.
- BusyBlocks and DailyFlow-created events are different concepts and must remain logically separated.
- BusyBlocks should represent occupied time from the user-selected Google calendars.
- Reuse existing Google OAuth/token refresh logic where possible.
- Current Google scopes should preserve both:
  - https://www.googleapis.com/auth/calendar.readonly
  - https://www.googleapis.com/auth/calendar.app.created
- If Google reconnect is triggered from a specific screen, the user should return to the same source screen after OAuth when possible.
- If implementing a return_to parameter for OAuth, only allow safe internal frontend paths and default to /calendar when missing or invalid.
- Do not create an open redirect risk.

Calendar / scheduling UI rules:
- App-owned displayed times should use 24-hour HH:mm format.
- Do not show AM/PM in DailyFlow UI.
- Add-to-calendar popups in Meals and Workouts should use controlled 24-hour HH:mm input if native browser time input displays AM/PM.
- In Meals and Workouts add popups, selectable days should be only from today through Saturday of the current week, inclusive.
- Day labels should always be in English and should use this format:
  - Sunday 10.05
  - Monday 11.05
- Do not allow selecting past days from the current week.
- Do not change actual ISO datetime values sent to Google Calendar unless needed to derive them correctly from the selected date/time.

Profile/settings rules:
- Screens should use the shared profile/preferences source.
- Do not create duplicate local preference state if existing profile data can be reused.
- Preferences changed in one screen should be reflected in other screens after save/navigation.
- Avoid adding new onboarding questionnaire questions unless explicitly requested.
- Keep real error messages for failed save/load/validation.
- Remove unnecessary helper notes or cluttered microcopy from the Profile/Preferences popup when requested.
- Profile and Preferences popup/modal should have consistent width and stable size between sections.
- Do not reintroduce Meal Preferences.

Workouts rules:
- Workouts implementation should remain stable and not be rewritten unless explicitly requested.
- Workout generation should use saved preferences and available free time.
- Existing saved/approved workout plan items should not disappear after Generate.
- Items added to Google Calendar should remain marked as added.
- Add to calendar must not create duplicate Google events.
- Delete should remove the linked DailyFlow-created event when applicable.
- Do not change Workouts while working on Meals unless the requested task explicitly depends on shared code.
- Workout UI should stay consistent with Meals where appropriate, including subtle icons and pastel tag/category styling.
- If adding icons, use clean UI icons or inline SVGs, not emoji.

